obably  pissed off and tired of living beyond  the wall for thousands of years when the  children made the night King the  ceremony included those same seven lines  of stones in a spiral pattern with the  person dead senator since they are  reproducing that symbol it might be his  way to tell people that he remembers and  it's a reminder to those who also use  these symbols after all he made us be  arraigned a man that got kidnapped and  transformed into a white Walker  everything was taken away from him by  the children so in his mind he's the  good guy who once revenge they could be  leaving these as a message to the  children of the forest this would let  the children know that he's back and  he's coming for them but that's just a  guess these symbols aren't the only  thing the White Walkers have adapted  they have also used another pattern that  we see in the very first episode of the  series as well when Ned Stark beheads  the man from the Nights Watch there is a  circular pattern of stones around the  stump where the man is placed in the  center this symbol is also seen when the  knight King turns the baby into a white  Walker there are large pieces of ice in  a circular pattern with a block in the  senator since the knight King is also  using these symbols this could be  another hint at the knight Kings  northern routes the knight king  ceremonial grounds remind me of the  Starks ned uses his location to end life  while the knight King uses his to  possibly give eternal life it's very  interesting  there is also that scene in the cave on  Dragonstone in the scene john leads Dany  into the caves to check out these cave  paintings created by none other than the  children of the forest  they were here together the children in  the first man doing what fighting each  other  [Music]  in the paintings we see what's assumed  to be the war for the dawn a  generational long battle where the first  men and the children teamed up against a  White Walkers during the scen